{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>They acted foolishly.</b> Like אשר נואלנו (we have acted foolishly) (Numbers 12:11), in the sense of folly." "<b>They seduced.</b> From the root of הנחש השיאני (the serpent beguiled me) (Genesis 3:13), in the nifal binyan." "<b>The chiefs of its tribes.</b> They are the great ones, like פנות כל העם (the corners of all the people) (Judges 3:2):" "And the meaning of שבטיה is the families."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:19.329015493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}